          <p>
            If your sealed attic runs warm, the AlorAir units have the most headroom. If it stays close to the house temperature, the Santa Fe and AprilAire machines are more efficient and better built for ducting. Either way, a sealed attic that regularly exceeds 100°F is a sign the foam is too thin or the attic is not as sealed as it should be, and that deserves fixing before you buy equipment.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Cold-Climate Limits</h3>

          <p>
            Cold matters less in most climates, because a sealed attic in winter sits near indoor temperature and humidity loads are low. In a cold climate where a sealed attic can drop into the 40s, the AprilAire units' 50°F inlet minimum and the Santa Fe's 49°F floor mean they will sit idle on the coldest days, which is usually fine. If you need dehumidification in a cold, unheated space, see our <a href="/best-desiccant-dehumidifier/">desiccant dehumidifier guide</a>.
          </p>
